>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

Explanation of the change:

- Original regex `\(\*[\s\S]*?\*\)` happily matches `(*)` (zero characters in the middle), so your `(*)` operator gets eaten as a comment.
- By changing `*?` (zero-or-more) to `+?` (one-or-more), we ensure Prism only treats `(* … *)` as a comment when there’s actually something inside it. Now `(*)` remains intact and gets correctly tokenized as operator syntax.
